    {
      "id": "claim_aaf7481e08ab47a5b547300db3f8c211",
      "statement": "The Sensorboard only ever opens a GATT connection to a GasBee for calibration (zero-point, reference weight, raw offset/scale) and tare commands while that GasBee is on USB in configuration mode, handled by gasbee_gatt_cal.c which connects by MAC, writes the characteristic, and disconnects immediately; normal weight/battery/status ingestion is done exclusively via passive advertising scan, never GATT, and while a GATT connection is open the GasBee sends no advertising bursts so no new weight values are received during that time.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://firmware/gasbee_nrf/README.md#L95-L99",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:49901f42f1104ad36ee4c7d34830ce5af0050a5fef023cbeff25d895fbb15819:"
        },
